1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,321
AI agents can read thousands of pages,

2
00:00:03,321 --> 00:00:08,351
but the creators whose evidence shapes
an answer usually receive nothing.

3
00:00:08,351 --> 00:00:09,723
Keryx changes that.

4
00:00:09,723 --> 00:00:14,753
A user asks a question and sets a hard
USDC budget.

5
00:00:14,753 --> 00:00:17,953
The agent discovers sources, explains
every buy,

6
00:00:17,953 --> 00:00:22,526
skip, and cache decision, buys only the
evidence it values,

7
00:00:22,526 --> 00:00:26,184
cites what survives verification, and
pays those creators.

8
00:00:27,104 --> 00:00:29,804
This is the entire economic loop.

9
00:00:29,804 --> 00:00:34,754
The browser holds the session key and
funds a capped Circle

10
00:00:34,754 --> 00:00:35,654
Gateway balance.

11
00:00:35,654 --> 00:00:40,605
Keryx decomposes the question, discovers articles
from the on-chain Source Registry,

12
00:00:40,605 --> 00:00:42,855
and prices each exact version.

13
00:00:42,855 --> 00:00:47,355
An X four oh two access toll unlocks
selected content.

14
00:00:47,355 --> 00:00:50,505
After synthesis, the evidence gate
measures contribution.

15
00:00:50,505 --> 00:00:54,555
A second, weighted reward goes only to
cited sources.

16
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:59,055
The cap, decisions, payments, and
settlement state remain visible throughout.

17
00:00:59,975 --> 00:01:03,916
Here is a real public dispatch on Arc
testnet.

18
00:01:03,916 --> 00:01:08,733
The agent was asked how long X four oh
two payments

19
00:01:08,733 --> 00:01:11,798
take to finalize, with a five-cent
ceiling.

20
00:01:11,798 --> 00:01:16,615
It discovered candidates, rejected sources that
were off-topic or too expensive,

21
00:01:16,615 --> 00:01:18,804
and bought three relevant pieces.

22
00:01:18,804 --> 00:01:22,307
The trace records the reason for every
choice.

23
00:01:22,307 --> 00:01:25,811
It stopped within budget, produced a
cited answer,

24
00:01:25,811 --> 00:01:29,314
and allocated the citation pool by
measured contribution:

25
00:01:29,314 --> 00:01:32,379
forty percent, forty percent, and twenty
percent.

26
00:01:33,299 --> 00:01:36,850
Payment is not a decorative success
badge.

27
00:01:36,850 --> 00:01:41,417
Each purchased article first returned
HTTP four oh two.

28
00:01:41,417 --> 00:01:44,968
Keryx authorized the exact network, USDC
asset,

29
00:01:44,968 --> 00:01:50,549
amount, and creator-controlled payee, then retried
with the signed payment header.

30
00:01:50,549 --> 00:01:56,130
Circle Gateway returned settlement references for
the access tolls and citation

31
00:01:56,130 --> 00:01:56,637
rewards.

32
00:01:56,637 --> 00:02:00,189
The completed dispatch preserves the
answer, citations,

33
00:02:00,189 --> 00:02:03,740
spend, and receipts as one audit trail.

34
00:02:04,660 --> 00:02:07,923
The code uses Circle's official packages
directly.

35
00:02:07,923 --> 00:02:13,051
In real gateway dot T S, Batch E V M
Scheme

36
00:02:13,051 --> 00:02:16,780
and Gateway Client connect the buyer to
Arc.

37
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:20,975
In X four oh two server dot T S,

38
00:02:20,975 --> 00:02:24,239
each challenge binds the Arc network,
USDC,

39
00:02:24,239 --> 00:02:28,900
integer micro-USDC amount, creator pay-to
address, and Gateway verifying contract.

40
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:33,095
The seller verifies and settles before
serving paid content.

41
00:02:33,095 --> 00:02:36,824
Unified Balance Kit powers the public
treasury view.

42
00:02:36,824 --> 00:02:41,952
These are the production integration
points reviewers can inspect in the

43
00:02:41,952 --> 00:02:45,215
repository and validate in the running
product.

44
00:02:46,135 --> 00:02:49,146
For browser users, Keryx remains
non-custodial.

45
00:02:49,146 --> 00:02:54,667
Before a bearer authorization can exist,
the server atomically reserves the

46
00:02:54,667 --> 00:02:57,177
amount against the session cap.

47
00:02:57,177 --> 00:03:01,694
The browser independently validates the
challenge and co-signs it.

48
00:03:01,694 --> 00:03:07,214
After submission, missing confirmation is pending,
never quietly marked failed or

49
00:03:07,214 --> 00:03:07,716
settled.

50
00:03:07,716 --> 00:03:11,731
Payout authority comes from Source
Registry on Arc,

51
00:03:11,731 --> 00:03:14,241
not an editable database row.

52
00:03:14,241 --> 00:03:19,762
Finally, run agent dot T S allocates
every citation reward in

53
00:03:19,762 --> 00:03:25,282
integer micro-USDC, including multi-author splits, so
the payment legs add up

54
00:03:25,282 --> 00:03:25,784
exactly.

55
00:03:26,704 --> 00:03:30,965
The proof pages separate scale from
adoption.

56
00:03:30,965 --> 00:03:37,662
At this production snapshot, Keryx has
settled 9,527 payments and 45.

